<p>Use this tab to configure further advanced options for printing.</p>
<p>Available functions differ depending on the printer or printer driver 
 you are using.</p>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Manage One Click Presets</span></p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="manage" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Manage...</span></p>
<p>Opens the <span class="Term-Soft">Manage One Click Preset List</span> 
 dialog box to specify a one click preset name and comment, or change the 
 display order. You can also share registered one click presets among users 
 and delete existing one click presets.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="donot" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Do not Allow User to Register Preset</span></p>
<p>Prohibits users from registering one click presets.</p>
<p>When users open <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used Settings</span> 
 Tab or <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> Tab, <span class="Term-Soft">Register 
 Current Settings...</span> is grayed out, users cannot register new one 
 click presets.</p>
<p>Users cannot specify a one click preset name and comment, nor change 
 the display order in the <span class="Term-Soft">Manage One Click Preset 
 List</span> dialog box (Printing Preferences).</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="notchange" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Do not allow changing the display 
 order in One Click Preset List</span></p>
<p>Prohibits users from changing the order of the system-provided and shared 
 one click presets. Users can only change the order of the one click presets 
 they register. If you clear the check box, you can change the order of 
 all kinds of one click presets.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="auth2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">User Authentication...</span></p>
<p>Open the <span class="Term-Soft">User Authentication</span> dialog box to set the user authentication settings.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="jobtypecode" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Job Type/Code Dialog Settings...</span></p>
<p>Open the <span class="Term-Soft">Job Type/Code Dialog Settings</span> dialog box to set the printing method for printing.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="securityset" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Security Settings...</span></p>
<p>Open the <span class="Term-Soft">Security Settings</span> dialog box to set whether to encrypt print data.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="increase" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Increase Auto-keep Settings for Applications</span></p>
<p>Select the check box to apply the print settings of the previous sheet 
 when using an application such as Microsoft® Excel®.</p>
<p><img alt="" class="help-img" height="179" loading="lazy" src="~/images/help/Bappli.gif" width="330"/></p>
<ol>
<li><p>Make the print settings for the first of the four 
 sheets of data.</p></li>
<li><p>These print settings are applied to the remaining 
 three sheets.</p></li>
</ol>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="collatedevice" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Collate by Device</span></p>
<p>If you cannot use the collate function because the optional hard disk 
 or additional memory is not installed in the printer, clear this check 
 box to have the prints sorted into sets according to the application collate 
 settings.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="notify" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Notify application that both dmPaperLength and dmPaperWidth are not supported</span></p>
<p>Select the check box to turn off dmPaperLength and dmPaperWidth for DC_FIELDS and dmFields in the driver.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="custom" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Register Custom Paper Size...</span></p>
<p>Opens the <span class="Term-Soft">Register Custom Paper Size</span> dialog 
 box, where you can register custom paper sizes.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="default" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Restore Defaults</span></p>
<p>Restores the settings on this tab to the default settings.</p>
